From: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 18:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: qcs6490-imdt-sbc: detach eMMC inline crypto

The IMDT QCS6490 SBC boots from the on-SoM eMMC (sdhc_1), not UFS. On this
Gunyah/LA firmware the SDCC1 inline-crypto engine (ICE, crypto@7c8000) is left
owned by TrustZone: UEFI's CryptoDxe only fixes up the UFS ICE, and on an
eMMC-only board it finds no UFS node --

  CryptoDxeFixupEventNotifyFunc: ufs node not found in device tree

so the SDCC1 ICE is never handed to the HLOS. When the sdhci-msm driver probes
sdhc_1 and programs the ICE, the access is rejected and the SoC takes an
immediate PSHOLD warm reset during probe (last console line is the
"sdhci_msm 7c4000.mmc: there are no valid maps for state default" note, then
the board resets and eventually drops into ramdump/EDL).

This board does not need inline storage encryption, so detach the ICE from the
eMMC controller. With this the board boots to userspace.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: William Bright <william.bright@imd-tec.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-imdt-sbc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qcs6490-imdt-sbc.dts
@@ -617,6 +617,17 @@
 
 /* On-SoM 32 GB eMMC */
 &sdhc_1 {
+	/*
+	 * This board boots from eMMC, not UFS. UEFI's CryptoDxe only fixes up
+	 * (unlocks) the UFS inline-crypto engine -- the boot log shows
+	 * "CryptoDxeFixupEventNotifyFunc: ufs node not found in device tree" --
+	 * so the SDCC1 ICE at 0x7c8000 is left owned by TrustZone. When the HLOS
+	 * sdhci-msm driver then touches the ICE the SoC takes an immediate
+	 * warm reset during probe. We have no need for inline storage encryption
+	 * here, so detach the ICE from the controller.
+	 */
+	/delete-property/ qcom,ice;
+
 	vmmc-supply = <&vreg_l7b_2p952>;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vreg_l19b_1p8>;
 
